  "verbalization": "Amoxicillin is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared pathway involving beta-lactam antibiotics, with multiple evidence chains converging on the same core mechanism. The evidence suggests that Amoxicillin, as a beta-lactam antibiotic, binds to Slc22a6 through a common ancestor relationship with Nafcillin, which itself binds to Slc22a6. This indicates a potential mechanism where beta-lactam antibiotics, through a shared structural or functional relationship, interact with Slc22a6. The integration of multiple paths highlights that the relationship is not unique to Amoxicillin but is part of a broader class of beta-lactam antibiotics, which may share similar interactions with Slc22a6. The evidence supports a dependency on beta-lactam antibiotics for the interaction with Slc22a6, suggesting a possible role in drug resistance or transport regulation.",
